  "question": {
    "text": "A uniform electric field and a uniform magnetic field are acting along the same direction in a certain region. If an electron is projected along the direction of the fields with a certain velocity then",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "TanWM",
      "text": "\nits velocity will decrease.\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "zhDfB",
      "text": "\nits velocity will increase.\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "KhTy9",
      "text": "\n it will turn towards right of direction of motion.\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "lVrde",
      "text": "\nit will turn towards left of direction of motion",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\vec{F}=-e[\\vec{E}+\\vec{v} \\times \\vec{B}]=-e \\vec{E}$\n$\\vec{a}=-\\frac{e \\vec{E}}{m}$\n$v(t)=v_{\\circ}-\\frac{e E}{m} t$",
